INCLUDING:  All full-time and regular part-time assembly department and machine shop employees, including assemblers and honing operators, CNC operators and CNC/set up operators, tool crib attendants and machine shop leads and CNC operator/Shift leads employed by the Employer at its facility currently located at 794 North Cypress Street, Orange, California 92867;

EXCLUDING:  All other employees, office clerical employees, professional employees, managerial employees, confidential employees, guards, and supervisors as defined in the Act.

Others permitted to vote: The parties have agreed that Receiving Inspectors, Layout Inspectors, and Final Inspectors employed by the Employer at its facility currently located at 794 North Cypress Street, Orange, California 92867 may vote in the election, but their ballots will be challenged since their eligibility has not been resolved.  No decision has been made regarding whether the individuals in these classifications or groups are included in, or excluded from, the bargaining unit.  The eligibility or inclusion of these individuals will be resolved, if necessary, following the election.

Included:  All full-time and regular part-time System Technicians, Electronics Technician Maintenance 2, Electronics Technician Maintenance 3, and Engineering Technician 5 employed by the Employer and working in the Water Craft Group, Power Distribution Group, and Target Shop Department in the SCI Support Section at the Southern California Offshore Range (SCORE), San Clemente Island;

Excluded:  All other employees, office clerical employees, professional employees, managerial employees, guards and supervisors as defined in the Act.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for the INTERNATIONAL ASSOCIATION OF MACHINISTS & AEROSPACE WORKERS, AFL-CIO, DISTRICT LODGE 725, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing certified unit in Case 21-RC-183551.  If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

